<title>ISRAEL: Israel grain, meal, soy arrivals detailed.</title>
<headline>Israel grain, meal, soy arrivals detailed.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following shipments of grain have arrived or are due to arrive in Israeli ports, according to the inspection agency Hevra Klalit Lehashgaha (in tonnes):</p>
<p>Vessel	     ETA	   Cargo	    Quantity   Origin</p>
<p>Europa	     unloading   corn	     20,500     U.S.</p>
<p>				     barley	   19,870</p>
<p>				     sunflower meal  3,600</p>
<p>Boris Zadanovsky unloading   wheat		 841     Europe</p>
<p>				     rapeseeds	   643</p>
<p>				     sunflower	   941</p>
<p>Volgobalt 234     arrived    barley	    2,879     Europe</p>
<p>Kafkametler	 4/6	  barley	    2,340     Europe</p>
<p>Fannie		5/6	  corn	     25,611     U.S</p>
<p>				     wheat	    13,000</p>
<p>Cengis K	    6/6	  gluten feed     8,000     U.S.</p>
<p>				     gluten meal     3,800</p>
<p>				     sorghum	   8,000</p>
<p>				     soya	     17,000</p>
<p>				     corn screening  6,000</p>
